Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Stained Glass OS -- Task Manager (sg-taskmgr), Windows 10's: taskmgr in the
; Run box, ShellExecute and the Win+X menu open it. Wine's own taskmgr.exe in
; system32 (what CreateProcess finds first) hands off to this App Paths entry
; in wine-sg.
;
; The path is the package's install location reached through Z:. If Z: is ever
; removed from the prefix for isolation, this must move with it.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\App Paths\taskmgr.exe]
@="Z:\\usr\\libexec\\stained-glass\\shell\\sg-taskmgr64.exe"
